   "source": [
    "# Spotify Music Pattern Analysis\n",
    "\n",
    "## tl;dr\n",
    "\n",
    "Across 89,741 unique tracks, audio features have only weak bivariate associations with popularity; the strongest is instrumentalness (Spearman Ï = **âˆ’0.124**). High-popularity tracks are less instrumental and acoustic, slightly more danceable, and louder on average. Seven exploratory audio clusters overlap substantially (silhouette = **0.195**)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "62424629",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Context & Methods\n",
    "\n",
    "The analysis asks which audio features are associated with popularity, how genre labels differ, and whether tracks form useful audio-style clusters.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Key Assumptions\n",
    "\n",
    "- A track may appear under multiple genre labels; track-level analyses deduplicate `track_id`.\n",
    "- Genre comparisons retain genre-tag rows because one track can legitimately contribute to multiple labels.\n",
    "- Popularity is a snapshot, not a time series or causal outcome."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "id": "d2f406ff",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
